{"id":"chatcmpl-513e3c1f-a44a-4ab5-8d7c-4f219eb14186","object":"chat.completion","created":1795251420,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a forced-choice medical imaging question conflicts with an initial expert tool's negative finding, the successful strategy was to triangulate with multiple independent visual-assessment tools and targeted region-of-interest crops rather than accept the first answer. Laterality on a lateral view was resolved by reasoning about anatomical landmarks (diaphragm height, posterior extent of lower lobes) and cross-checking across models. The pattern generalizes to any ambiguous visual QA where tools disagree and the answer format forces a commitment.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a tool reports 'no finding' but the question forces a choice, treat the negative as unreliable and seek independent confirmation from a second visual model before answering.\",\n    \"Use region-of-interest cropping/zoom on the specific anatomical area in question to enable direct visual inspection when whole-image assessments are ambiguous.\",\n    \"Resolve laterality or localization on views lacking standard landmarks by reasoning from anatomical priors (e.g., which structure sits higher or extends more posteriorly) rather than raw pixel position.\",\n    \"Triangulate across heterogeneous tools (specialist descriptor, general VQA, radiology-tuned model) and let the most specific, anatomy-grounded description drive the final answer when they conflict.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging forced-choice QA\": \"Never accept a single tool's negative when the format forbids 'none'; gather at least two independent visual assessments and one targeted crop before committing.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual localization\": \"Anchor laterality/side judgments in anatomical priors and landmark relationships, not image coordinates, especially on lateral or non-standard views.\",\n    \"Tool-disagreement resolution\": \"Weight the tool whose output is most anatomically specific and consistent with the cropped visual evidence; document the conflict in the reasoning.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding with at least two independent visual tools plus a zoomed crop of the relevant region before finalizing.\",\n    \"Verify laterality using anatomical landmarks (not pixel position) and ensure the chosen option matches the most specific positive description.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":848,"total_tokens":1278,"completion_tokens":430,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":848},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":430}}}